# Governance lever for "who owns canon".
#
# This file -- not the CMS config -- is what makes the core frozen or open.
# It is paired with the "Canon review" ruleset on main, which requires a code
# owner's approval for anything listed here. Without that ruleset this file is
# only a description.
#
# ORDER MATTERS, AND BACKWARDS. CODEOWNERS uses LAST-match-wins, unlike almost
# every other path-matching system in git. The specific rules therefore go at
# the BOTTOM. Written the intuitive way round -- specific first, general after
# -- the broad `/wiki/docs/` line silently overrode the frozen-rules line, and
# the one page ended up owned by whoever owned everything else. It looked
# correct and did nothing.
#
# Jeff has two accounts, both org admins. Either can approve.

# --- Everything in the site: any maintainer -----------------------------------
/wiki/docs/                    @doesplaydice/maintainers
/wiki/mkdocs.yml               @doesplaydice/maintainers
/kit/                          @doesplaydice/maintainers

# --- The open front door: no code owner, merges on normal review --------------
# Community modules are other people's work. Deliberately unowned so a
# contributor is not waiting on us to publish their own module.
/wiki/docs/community/

# --- Frozen core: the one page needs Jeff himself. LAST, so it wins. ----------
/wiki/docs/rules/index.md      @doesplaydice-user @thoughtsfired
